### TaxRateSystem - auth smoke tests (API.md §6, §17 Flows 1-2)
### The OTP codes arrive by e-mail; with MAIL_ENABLED=false they are written to the application log.
### Run the requests top to bottom: login/refresh/reset-verify capture the tokens the flow needs.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api/v1
@email = juan.delacruz@example.com
@password = SecurePassword123

### §6.1 - register (201; the 6-digit verification code arrives by e-mail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Juan",
  "lastName": "Dela Cruz",
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "phoneNumber": "09171234567",
  "address": {
    "street": "123 Rizal Avenue",
    "barangay": "Barangay 1",
    "city": "Manila",
    "province": "Metro Manila",
    "postalCode": "1000"
  }
}

### §6.2 - activate the account with the e-mailed code (200, status ACTIVE)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/verify-registration
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "code": "482913" }

### §6.3 - resend a code (200; identical answer whether or not the address exists)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/resend-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "purpose": "REGISTRATION" }

### §6.4 - login (200 with tokens; captures them for the later requests)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

> {%
    client.global.set("accessToken", response.body.accessToken);
    client.global.set("refreshToken", response.body.refreshToken);
%}

### §6.5 - refresh: rotates the token and issues a new pair
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}" }

> {%
    client.global.set("accessToken", response.body.accessToken);
    client.global.set("refreshToken", response.body.refreshToken);
%}

### §6.6 - logout (204). Access tokens stay valid until they expire; delete the stored pair.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}", "allDevices": false }

### §6.7 - password reset: request a code (200, same response for unknown addresses)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/password-reset/request
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}" }

### §6.8 - exchange the code for a single-use reset token (200, captures it)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/password-reset/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "code": "482913" }

> {%
    client.global.set("resetToken", response.body.resetToken);
%}

### §6.9 - set the new password (200; every session of the account is revoked)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/password-reset/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "resetToken": "{{resetToken}}",
  "newPassword": "SecurePassword456",
  "confirmPassword": "SecurePassword456"
}

